{
  "_about": "Annexe I of Ganiage 1966, p. 882: 'Les impositions a la mejba (d'apres le budget de 1277)'. Every fiscal unit of the Regency with the number of men assessed to the mejba poll tax, read off the page image by eye. 1277 AH runs from July 1860 to July 1861.",
  "_source": {
    "citation": "Jean Ganiage, 'La population de la Tunisie vers 1860. Essai d'evaluation d'apres les registres fiscaux', Population, 21e annee, n. 5, 1966, pp. 857-886",
    "doi": "10.2307/1528138",
    "url": "https://www.persee.fr/doc/pop_0032-4663_1966_num_21_5_13406",
    "page": 882,
    "page_image": "https://www.persee.fr/renderPage/pop_0032-4663_1966_num_21_5_13406/pop_0032-4663_1966_num_21_5_T1_0882_0000_1400.jpg",
    "unit": "men assessed to the mejba, not souls and not households"
  },
  "_how_read": "Persee's per-page text endpoint interleaves the two printed columns, so the name-to-number pairing it returns cannot be trusted and was not used. The page image was fetched at 1148 px wide and read by eye, left column top to bottom then right column, then every line was read a second time in four crops enlarged 2.6x. The TOTAL row was read a third time at 4x. The annexe is printed entirely on p. 882; p. 883 carries Annexe II and was not needed.",
  "_arithmetic": {
    "lines": 78,
    "lines_left_column": 40,
    "lines_right_column": 38,
    "sum_of_printed_lines": 215607,
    "printed_total": 221664,
    "difference": 6057,
    "_comment": "The printed TOTAL exceeds the sum of the printed lines by 6.057, or 2.7 per cent. The lines were verified twice and the total three times, so the gap is in the source rather than in the reading. Tunis itself is absent from the list, which is one candidate for what the total counts and the lines do not; the annexe does not say. Reported, not reconciled."
  },
  "_attribution": "'tribe' carries the gazetteer name only where the source says so. basis 'footnote' means one of Ganiage's fourteen footnotes ties the fiscal unit to a tribe; basis 'name' means the printed name is a gazetteer tribe on its own; basis 'none' means the line is a town, a district, an oasis group, a service corps or a tribe the gazetteer does not hold, and it is left unattributed. 'also_gazetteer' names a finer gazetteer entry the line matches on its own, and 'joint' marks a line whose figure covers two entries together.",
  "footnotes": {
    "1": "nom traditionnel du district du Cap Bon",
    "2": "Tribu des Zlass",
    "3": "groupe d'oasis du Djerid a l'est de Tozeur",
    "4": "petites oasis de montagne de la frontiere, a 65 km au nord de Tozeur",
    "5": "Tribu des Hammama",
    "6": "tribu fixee autour de Gafsa",
    "7": "Ouled Sidi Tlil, groupe rattache aux Frechich",
    "8": "tribu nomadisant au nord du Djerid entre Tozeur et Tamerza",
    "9": "Tribu des Frechich",
    "10": "Tribu des Majeur",
    "11": "tribu rattachee au caidat de la Kessera",
    "12": "tribus du nord-ouest de la ligue des Ounifa",
    "13": "tribu de service",
    "14": "Tripolitains fixes dans la basse vallee de la Medjerda"
  },
